# Page Builder — Core Architecture (always active)

You are building `@itzsa/page-builder`, a drag-and-drop visual page builder
(Elementor / Webflow / Puck class). The full design authority is
`ARCHITECTURE-PAGE-BUILDER.md` in the repo root. This file is a condensed,
enforceable summary. When in doubt, re-read that doc before writing code.

## Non-negotiables (ADR-01 through ADR-14)

1. **One render path.** Every block has exactly one React `render` component.
   Canvas iframe, Preview, and Open Page all mount it from the registry.
   Never create a second HTML template, a `*.render.ts` string builder, or a
   parallel "publish" component for the same block type.

2. **Canvas ≠ decorated preview.** The engine does NOT ship decorative CSS
   for blocks (no default card/hero/button skins, no "looks nice out of the
   box" padding/shadows). Look comes ONLY from author-written `customCss` /
   `globalCss`. If you're tempted to add a default style so a block "looks
   less empty" in the canvas — don't. That is the exact CIB bug this
   architecture exists to fix.

3. **Editor chrome lives in the parent document, never inside the page DOM.**
   Selection outlines, drag ghosts, hover rings, toolbars = parent-rendered
   overlays positioned via `canvasBridge` measurements. They must never be
   injected into the iframe's page document or affect its visual contract.

4. **Data ≠ behavior.** `Page` / `Block` JSON never contains render
   functions. `BlockDefinition` (registry) never contains page content.
   No block type may be special-cased with `switch (block.type)` outside
   the registry dispatcher itself.

5. **Host owns I/O.** The engine never imports host `services/`, `store/`,
   or `routes/`. All persistence, auth, uploads, and data fetching happen
   through injected callbacks (`onSave`, `onPublish`, `uploadAsset`,
   `fetchDynamicBlocks`, `fetchDataSource`, `capabilities`, `renderContext`).
   If a task seems to require reaching into host internals, stop and flag it.

6. **Composition over mega-widgets.** Do not build monolithic composite
   blocks (`hero`, `blog-card`, etc.) as the primary way to express complex
   UI. Compose from primitives (`box`/`container`, `heading`, `text`,
   `image`, `button`, `flex`, `grid`, `repeater`). Composites are only
   allowed for tightly-coupled interactive widgets that truly cannot be
   expressed as a tree (rare) — and even then must use the same
   registry/render/CSS rules.

7. **Persist JSON by default (ADR-14).** The canonical saved document is
   always the structured `Page` JSON, schema-validated. Full HTML is an
   OPTIONAL derived export via the same `RenderPage` path — never the
   source of truth for re-opening the editor. If both exist, JSON wins on
   conflict.

8. **No eval, ever.** Block `render` functions are never created via
   `eval`, `new Function`, or unsigned remote script injection. See the
   registry rule file for Model A / Model B constraints.

## Parity rule (test this constantly)

If something is visible as page content in the canvas for the current
`renderContext`, it MUST render identically in Preview and Open Page.
Before considering any canvas-affecting change "done," ask: does this still
hold for Preview and Open Page with the same JSON + author CSS + active
locale?

## Hard rules checklist — verify before finishing ANY task

- [ ] Canvas === Preview === Open Page for same JSON + CSS + locale + renderContext
- [ ] No decorative CSS added by the engine
- [ ] Editor chrome stays in parent overlays only
- [ ] Same React `render` used by all three surfaces
- [ ] No `switch` on block type outside registry dispatch
- [ ] Primitives + presets/repeater preferred over new composite block types
- [ ] Delete / copy / paste / duplicate / outline stay history-aware
- [ ] Translatable fields use `i18nProps`; flat host keys normalize through `i18nResolve`, never a hardcoded `switch (lang)`
- [ ] Preview URL contains only an opaque id/key — never serialized page JSON
- [ ] Custom CSS/JS only ever passes through composers, never raw-injected
- [ ] `styles.module.css` is editor-chrome only, never page look
- [ ] Live registry `.refine()` for `Block.type` — no frozen static enum
- [ ] Engine does not import host `services/` / `store/` / `routes/`
- [ ] New public capability gets a matching topic doc in the same PR

## When unsure

If a request would require deviating from this file (e.g. "just hardcode
this locale switch for now," "add a quick default CSS so it looks better"),
say so explicitly and propose the compliant alternative instead of silently
complying.
